        "title": "fix(config): accept agents.defaults.compaction.enabled",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Add `agents.defaults.compaction.enabled` to the public config type, Zod schema, labels, and help text so `enabled: false` validates instead of rejecting the whole config.\n- Wire the flag through `applyAgentAutoCompactionGuard` so proactive embedded auto-compaction can be disabled while overflow recovery, OpenClaw preemptive overflow handling, and manual `/compact` remain available.\n- Document the setting in `docs/concepts/compaction.md` and regenerate the config baseline hash.\n\nFixes #110065.\n\n## Change type\n- Bug fix\n\n## Touched areas\n- Config schema / agent defaults\n- Embedded agent auto-compaction guard\n- Docs\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/agent-settings.test.ts src/config/zod-schema.agent-defaults.test.ts src/config/schema.help.quality.test.ts` (101 tests passed)\n- [x] `node --import tsx scripts/generate-base-config-schema.ts --check`\n- [x] `node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --write` (hash updated)\n\n## Root cause\n`AgentCompactionConfig` / strict Zod compaction object omitted top-level `enabled`, while session settings already expose `compaction.enabled`. Users setting `agents.defaults.compaction.enabled: false` hit `Invalid config`.\n\n## Security impact\n- No auth/credential/sandbox changes.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
